    "answer": {
      "short": "$d=0.8$, so a $20\\%$ decrease.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}100\\times1.25\\times d&=100\\\\125d&=100\\\\d&=\\frac{100}{125}\\\\d&=0.8\\end{align*}$$\nThe multiplier $0.8$ leaves $80\\%$ of the increased price, so the required decrease is $100\\%-80\\%=20\\%$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
